`28`. Prices were losing a cent before any totals were calculated, so the subtotal and every number built on it was wrong.\n\n**Fix:** `to_cents` now converts with `Decimal(str(amount)) * 100` and rounds half up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), the same rounding rule the discount and tax code already use. Converting through `str()` keeps the price as typed (`19.99`) instead of the float's long binary value.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- A price with more than two decimals (e.g. `0.125`) now rounds half up to 13 cents. Before, it was cut down to 12.\n- Very long float strings still work. `str()` gives the shortest exact form of the float, so the result is correct for any finite float.\n- `NaN` or `inf` now raises an error from `quantize`. Before, `int()` raised an error for these too.\n\nThe real fix would be to hold prices as `Decimal` or as integer cents from the start, not as floats. That would change the `Line` interface, so I left it alone.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 8, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 115168, "requests_cache_write": 46987, "requests_cost_usd": 0.2938406, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 18, "requests_output": 1790, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial3", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 5, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-12T23:42:51.431785+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 24.65, "t_checker_s": 0.38, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1808, "tokens_cache_read": 115168, "tokens_cache_write": 46987, "tokens_fresh": 1808, "tokens_input_uncached": 18, "tokens_main_cache_read": 115168, "tokens_main_cache_write": 46987, "